Shared memory helpers for vo_x11 and vo_xv.

XShm 1.2 passes a file descriptor to the X server instead of using a
SysV segment, so the memory stays owned by the client's uid and does
not need to be mode 777. The fd is handed over to xcb, which closes it
once the request is sent. fd passing is only tried over a unix socket.
SysV shared memory is used when the server, the connection or the
build does not support fd passing. The SysV attach is checked, so a
server that cannot access the segment (e.g. over TCP) makes us fall
back to plain XPutImage/XvPutImage.

Index: libvo/x11_common.c
